   "line": 58,
   "message": "rule_token strips every non-word character from both ends of the first word. A rule that is all punctuation becomes the empty string. The old code kept such a rule as written and raised on an empty one, which the 'unreadable' guard caught. Now two unrelated punctuation-only rules compare equal, and so do two empty ones. Fix: treat an empty rule_token on either side as unreadable (unwaived) rather than comparing it.",
